{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuspendingClock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","text":"Example"},{"code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"text":") when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"text":" passes between elements, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any error the upstream throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Throws"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/assertnofailure\/timeout(_:customerror:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fails if the sequence goes the given duration without producing an element, measured on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"t